ressbook><name>YASUI, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWATA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ORITA KATSUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANO KENTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUI SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWATA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ORITA, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, KENTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUI, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic compound which, when applied to an organic dye compound, can improve the light resistance without substantially impairing its desirable optical properties and which is excellent in solubility in organic solvents and compatibility with dyes. It is a formazan metal complex containing a specific formazan compound as a ligand. Also provided are: a process for producing the formazan metal complex; a light resistance improver comprising the formazan metal complex; an optical recording medium; a light absorber; and a formazan compound as an intermediate for producing the formazan metal complex.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un composé organique qui, lorsqu'on l'applique à un composé colorant organique, permet d'améliorer sa résistance à la lumière sans incidence sensible sur ses propriétés optiques, et qui est excellent en termes de solubilité dans les solvants organiques et de compatibilité avec les teintures. Ce complexe métallique de formazan renferme un composé formazan spécifique en tant que ligand. L'invention concerne également les aspects suivants : procédé de fabrication du complexe métallique de formazan ; support d'enregistrement optique ; absorbeur de lumière ; et composé à base de fromazan en tant qu'intermédiaire pour l'obtention du complexe métallique de formazan.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>